Mesh: preserve the shared light-map texture list's original order.

The LIGHTMAPS_SHARED (0xB026) writer derives the texture list from the light-maps
themselves, so it can only ever emit them in first-reference order. ZenGin's order
is not derivable that way: in the retail Gothic II NewWorld the first light-map
references texture 125, the second texture 1 and the third texture 125 again, so
the on-disk list is the order the light-map compiler created the textures in. The
list read by load() is therefore kept on Mesh::shared_lightmap_textures and reused
by save() when it still covers every light-map, which makes the chunk byte-identical
on a round trip; a mesh built from scratch (or whose light-maps were re-assigned)
still falls back to first-reference order.

diff --git a/include/zenkit/Mesh.hh b/include/zenkit/Mesh.hh
index 7148881..99b86bd 100644
--- a/include/zenkit/Mesh.hh
+++ b/include/zenkit/Mesh.hh
@@ -125,6 +125,14 @@ namespace zenkit {
 		/// \brief All shared light-maps associated with this mesh
 		std::vector<LightMap> lightmaps {};
 
+		/// \brief The shared light-map textures in their on-disk order.
+		///
+		/// ZenGin stores the light-map textures as a list which each light-map indexes into. That order is the one
+		/// the light-map compiler created the textures in and cannot be derived from the light-maps, so it is kept
+		/// here to allow #save to reproduce it. Empty for a mesh which was not loaded from a file; #save then falls
+		/// back to the order in which the light-maps first reference their textures.
+		std::vector<std::shared_ptr<Texture>> shared_lightmap_textures {};
+
 		std::vector<Polygon> geometry {};
 		std::vector<uint32_t> polygon_vertex_indices;
 		std::vector<uint32_t> polygon_feature_indices;
